# Merge into /etc/nut/upsd.conf on the PRIMARY (eulerpi5) — exposes upsd on the LAN.
#
# The default install listens on localhost only. Secondaries (mt/spark) reach
# upsd over TCP/3493, so the primary must also LISTEN on its LAN address.
#
# CRITICAL — a LISTEN change needs a FULL restart, not a reload:
#
#     systemctl restart nut-server
#
# `systemctl reload nut-server` is a NO-OP for LISTEN: upsd only binds its
# sockets at start, so a reload leaves it still bound to localhost only and the
# secondaries never connect (RESEARCH.md pitfall 1). The `monitor add` CLI does
# the full restart for you; this snippet is the operator reference / rollback.
#
# Keep the existing localhost lines so local upsc/upsmon on the primary still
# work, and add the LAN address. Least privilege: expose only the primary's own
# LAN IP, never 0.0.0.0.

LISTEN 127.0.0.1 3493
LISTEN ::1 3493
LISTEN 192.168.1.125 3493
